WEBVTT

00:00:28.240 --> 00:00:30.240
<i>Say goodbye, hello</i>

00:00:30.240 --> 00:00:35.480
<i>Then we repeat, going</i>
<i>eternally round and round</i>

00:00:35.480 --> 00:00:43.020
<i>Where will our path lead?</i>

00:00:43.020 --> 00:00:49.530
<i>What do I lose sight of when I'm with you?</i>

00:00:49.530 --> 00:00:57.200
<i>A colorful array of love and kindness</i>

00:00:57.200 --> 00:01:03.870
<i>I've remembered what</i>
<i>I'd forgotten since the days</i>

00:01:03.870 --> 00:01:10.180
<i>when we hurt each other over trivial things</i>

00:01:10.180 --> 00:01:17.450
<i>The sounds of our footsteps are</i>
<i>the "tracks" that lead to the future</i>

00:01:17.450 --> 00:01:25.190
<i>Within the ever-changing scenery... always</i>

00:01:25.190 --> 00:01:27.230
<i>Say goodbye, hello</i>

00:01:27.230 --> 00:01:32.300
<i>Then we repeat, going</i>
<i>eternally round and round</i>

00:01:32.300 --> 00:01:39.380
<i>This melody that paints the future,</i>
<i>until the world changes</i>

00:01:39.380 --> 00:01:41.380
<i>Say goodbye, hello</i>

00:01:41.380 --> 00:01:46.580
<i>The sun always rises again,</i>
<i>eternally repeating its arc</i>

00:01:46.580 --> 00:01:57.430
<i>It lights up our path</i>

00:02:04.470 --> 00:02:07.270
Never figured <i>you</i> for the one behind this.

00:02:07.270 --> 00:02:09.770
Valic's instincts are worthy of some notice.

00:02:09.770 --> 00:02:14.240
Rianshel... Agrazume... Faroid...

00:02:14.240 --> 00:02:16.150
Who's next?

00:02:16.150 --> 00:02:18.580
Gatol? Valic?

00:02:30.090 --> 00:02:31.920
Or is it me?

00:02:35.200 --> 00:02:37.670
I'd like to take my time enjoying this,

00:02:37.670 --> 00:02:39.860
but I can't stay too long.

00:03:44.830 --> 00:03:50.410
Oh, Mr. Shinmyou... starting next week,
recycling pickup will be on Mondays.

00:03:50.410 --> 00:03:52.240
Don't get confused, okay?

00:03:55.610 --> 00:03:57.680
Oh my, you didn't know?

00:03:57.680 --> 00:04:01.280
No, I heard. The nonburnable trash is Tuesdays,

00:04:01.280 --> 00:04:04.520
and the burnable trash is
Wednesdays and Fridays, right?

00:04:04.520 --> 00:04:08.420
You're awfully pale. Are you feeling sick?

00:04:08.420 --> 00:04:09.590
Yes, a little.

00:04:09.590 --> 00:04:12.090
You should take care of your health.

00:04:12.090 --> 00:04:15.630
Single people just don't
look after themselves properly.

00:04:15.630 --> 00:04:17.620
Thank you, Ms. Takayama.

00:05:48.690 --> 00:05:52.400
I wish I had power like Birdy's...

00:05:52.400 --> 00:05:54.230
lxioran power?

00:05:54.230 --> 00:05:58.470
I mean, if I were lxioran, people
wouldn't make fools of us like this...

00:05:58.470 --> 00:06:02.670
Being lxioran isn't as good as you think.

00:06:02.670 --> 00:06:03.670
Huh?

00:06:03.670 --> 00:06:08.310
lxiorans have lost many things to gain that power.

00:06:08.310 --> 00:06:09.880
What do you mean?

00:06:09.880 --> 00:06:13.320
It's something you don't need to understand yet.

00:06:13.320 --> 00:06:15.690
But remember one <i>thing:</i>

00:06:15.690 --> 00:06:21.490
for everything you gain,
you lose something... and vice versa.

00:06:21.490 --> 00:06:26.890
But... I want to become strong.
I want to protect Birdy.

00:06:41.010 --> 00:06:43.380
I'm very sorry, Colonel.

00:06:43.380 --> 00:06:48.080
It wasn't your fault. I underestimated him, too.

00:06:48.080 --> 00:06:49.120
Does it hurt?

00:06:49.120 --> 00:06:53.110
It's a nostalgic pain... the pain of the battlefield.

00:07:01.700 --> 00:07:03.400
Major Gatol, it's all over for me...

00:07:03.400 --> 00:07:06.800
Don't speak, Moss.
We're almost at the collection point.

00:07:08.140 --> 00:07:10.570
You still have work left to do for me.

00:07:12.740 --> 00:07:14.570
I won't let you die easily.

00:07:19.580 --> 00:07:25.580
You and I were the only survivors of
the campaign to subdue Planet Kaltago...

00:07:27.320 --> 00:07:30.320
It's rare for you to talk about old times, Colonel.

00:07:34.400 --> 00:07:36.230
So you're finally here.

00:07:38.070 --> 00:07:39.470
What happened?!

00:07:57.590 --> 00:08:00.780
<i>I tried to jump, so why...?</i>

00:08:21.710 --> 00:08:27.950
lxiorans aren't my field, so I only
know what I've heard in rumors.

00:08:27.950 --> 00:08:32.150
Close to thirty years ago,
there was apparently a project

00:08:32.150 --> 00:08:34.690
to develop lxiorans with "jump" abilities.

00:08:34.690 --> 00:08:37.230
But they pulled the plug on
the research pretty early on.

00:08:37.230 --> 00:08:38.890
Why?

00:08:38.890 --> 00:08:41.360
I heard that it was because
their success rate was so low,

00:08:41.360 --> 00:08:44.900
and most of their experimental subjects died.

00:08:44.900 --> 00:08:48.700
Even in their successful cases
the "jump" powers were uncertain,

00:08:48.700 --> 00:08:52.370
and the side effects of the experiments were severe.

00:08:52.370 --> 00:08:54.680
Did he really teleport?

00:08:54.680 --> 00:08:55.680
Definitely.

00:08:55.680 --> 00:08:58.710
Then he's out of our league.

00:08:58.710 --> 00:09:01.850
He'll kill us all for sure...

00:09:01.850 --> 00:09:05.190
Hmph! It's kill or be killed at this point.

00:09:05.190 --> 00:09:07.890
Why did you keep quiet about his abilities?

00:09:07.890 --> 00:09:12.700
The only thing I knew was
that he was a defective lxioran.

00:09:12.700 --> 00:09:16.200
This is the first I've heard
about him being able to jump.

00:09:16.200 --> 00:09:18.900
You go next.

00:09:18.900 --> 00:09:21.600
Go? You mean to Nataru?!

00:09:21.600 --> 00:09:22.870
Obviously.

00:09:22.870 --> 00:09:26.080
Colonel, would you please let me do it?

00:09:26.080 --> 00:09:29.250
I know my way around weapons better than he does.

00:09:29.250 --> 00:09:31.280
You're injured.

00:09:31.280 --> 00:09:34.720
It's nothing serious. Plus...

00:09:34.720 --> 00:09:37.710
I think this will make a good disguise.

00:09:43.060 --> 00:09:44.690
W-W-Wait...

00:09:47.760 --> 00:09:50.900
Crap... I'm gonna be late again...

00:09:50.900 --> 00:09:52.700
It's because you don't wake up early enough!

00:09:52.700 --> 00:09:55.940
Haven't you ever heard of
learning from your mistakes?

00:09:55.940 --> 00:09:58.210
"Learning from my mistakes"?

00:09:58.210 --> 00:10:00.200
Like <i>you're</i> one to talk!

00:10:03.480 --> 00:10:06.920
If you're an alien, I wish
you could at least teleport...

00:10:06.920 --> 00:10:10.450
Before you start grumbling, get to sprinting!

00:10:10.450 --> 00:10:11.650
Sheesh!

00:10:27.670 --> 00:10:30.810
He's probably in the rehabilitation center.

00:10:30.810 --> 00:10:33.410
It's at the end of the hall.

00:10:33.410 --> 00:10:35.240
Thank you.

00:10:36.180 --> 00:10:38.010
How are you feeling, Mr. Yoshida?

00:10:38.010 --> 00:10:40.150
It never ends.

00:10:40.150 --> 00:10:43.590
My lower back smarts, and nothing I do helps.

00:10:43.590 --> 00:10:47.190
It does take a while for lower back joints to heal.

00:10:47.190 --> 00:10:49.830
We just have to treat it patiently.

00:10:49.830 --> 00:10:52.450
Lie on your stomach and
relax your muscles, please.

00:10:54.500 --> 00:10:56.100
Okay, that's great.

00:10:56.100 --> 00:10:57.930
Now, here we go.

00:11:13.480 --> 00:11:15.470
Is this your first time here?

00:11:23.160 --> 00:11:25.150
What's the matter?

00:11:34.070 --> 00:11:35.900
Huh?

00:12:11.410 --> 00:12:16.580
O-Oh no! Mr. Shinmyou's disappeared!

00:12:16.580 --> 00:12:19.010
H-Hey, what was that for?!

00:12:19.010 --> 00:12:23.610
He was spirited away! A UFO erased Mr. Shinmyou!

00:12:25.720 --> 00:12:29.730
Amazing... Such amazing power...

00:12:29.730 --> 00:12:32.350
Such an amazing man...

00:12:34.460 --> 00:12:36.530
Hey, you're going to trip again.

00:12:36.530 --> 00:12:38.370
I'm fine!

00:12:38.370 --> 00:12:39.440
See?

00:12:39.440 --> 00:12:40.870
Hey...

00:12:46.880 --> 00:12:51.110
Sheesh, you're so clumsy for an lxioran.

00:12:51.110 --> 00:12:52.940
I'm going back in time...

00:13:03.160 --> 00:13:04.660
Stay here for a while, got it, Dad?

00:13:04.660 --> 00:13:07.900
It wouldn't be so bad to get captured by her.

00:13:07.900 --> 00:13:09.100
Give me a break!

00:13:09.100 --> 00:13:10.000
Dad...

00:13:10.000 --> 00:13:13.970
If you're going to say that now, then
you shouldn't have helped them escape!

00:13:13.970 --> 00:13:17.070
Run away. Run away from here!

00:13:17.070 --> 00:13:18.470
Dad!

00:13:42.360 --> 00:13:43.600
- What's going on?
- What is it?

00:13:43.600 --> 00:13:44.770
What was that?

00:13:44.770 --> 00:13:46.030
Hey, check it out!

00:13:46.030 --> 00:13:47.470
Wow...

00:13:50.940 --> 00:13:52.470
What happened?

00:13:52.470 --> 00:13:55.180
There's smoke coming up from the pond.

00:13:55.180 --> 00:13:57.980
Want to go take a look, and
skip out on this dumb class?

00:13:57.980 --> 00:13:58.810
Huh?

00:13:58.810 --> 00:14:02.890
Man, I'm just so freaking bored,
I've been wondering what to do.

00:14:02.890 --> 00:14:06.890
Yeah, maybe I picked the
wrong lecture to sign up for.

00:14:06.890 --> 00:14:08.060
Um...

00:14:08.060 --> 00:14:11.130
Yuichi Kagami, freshman, Economics Department.

00:14:11.130 --> 00:14:15.300
I'm Nataru Shinmyou. Freshman,
Education Department. Nice to meet you.

00:14:15.300 --> 00:14:16.500
What <i>was</i> that?

00:14:16.500 --> 00:14:20.700
- A firework, right?
- Is someone stupid enough to
set off a huge fireworks rocket here?

00:14:24.140 --> 00:14:26.880
Kanda, eh? Can I swing by on the way home?

00:14:26.880 --> 00:14:27.880
Sure...

00:14:27.880 --> 00:14:29.880
Wow, lots of people with free time, huh?

00:14:29.880 --> 00:14:31.710
Like you're one to talk!

00:14:31.710 --> 00:14:33.680
Whoa, you're more serious than I expected.

00:14:33.680 --> 00:14:36.250
Don't judge people by appearances.

00:14:36.250 --> 00:14:37.990
Yuichi...

00:14:37.990 --> 00:14:40.980
I'm hungry. Let's go grab something to eat.

00:14:44.690 --> 00:14:46.520
Kagami!

00:14:49.100 --> 00:14:50.930
Yuichi...

00:14:57.270 --> 00:15:00.410
What the heck? Today's recycling day!

00:15:00.410 --> 00:15:05.280
No, today's Wednesday! Burnable trash day!

00:15:05.280 --> 00:15:07.780
Huh?! Today is Wednesday?!

00:15:07.780 --> 00:15:11.410
Wednesday? It's... not Monday?

00:15:20.300 --> 00:15:21.520
Nataru?

00:15:23.700 --> 00:15:26.270
It looks like he's grown quite weak.

00:15:26.270 --> 00:15:30.870
I think he should go get a
thorough workup at a big hospital.

00:15:30.870 --> 00:15:33.270
Thank you so much for your trouble.

00:15:39.380 --> 00:15:42.250
He hasn't shown up at home or at the hospital.

00:15:42.250 --> 00:15:45.450
He probably got killed by the
bomb wherever he jumped to.

00:15:45.450 --> 00:15:47.890
I can't imagine he'd make such a mistake.

00:15:49.830 --> 00:15:51.330
Where's Tasera?

00:15:51.330 --> 00:15:55.260
She's completely lost her nerve, and
doesn't really answer pages anymore.

00:15:55.260 --> 00:15:57.970
She's probably afraid to
have people know where she is.

00:15:57.970 --> 00:16:02.600
In the end, she's just an Itan.
When things get bad, she runs...

00:16:10.980 --> 00:16:11.950
Nataru?!

00:16:11.950 --> 00:16:12.610
Yep.

00:16:12.610 --> 00:16:14.080
What happened the day before yesterday?

00:16:14.080 --> 00:16:16.990
You vanished so suddenly... I was really worried!

00:16:16.990 --> 00:16:22.420
Mr. Yoshida was flipping out about how
you disappeared right in front of him...

00:16:22.420 --> 00:16:25.030
He saw wrong; he's an old man.

00:16:25.030 --> 00:16:28.000
And you just up and took the day off yesterday...

00:16:28.000 --> 00:16:30.800
And I couldn't get you on the phone
no matter how many times I tried!

00:16:30.800 --> 00:16:32.700
I've got a lot going on right now.

00:16:32.700 --> 00:16:35.970
The truth is, I plan to quit.

00:16:35.970 --> 00:16:37.140
What?

00:16:37.140 --> 00:16:40.510
I might not be able to see you for a while, either.

00:16:40.510 --> 00:16:42.540
What do you mean?!

00:16:42.540 --> 00:16:45.980
You don't want to see me anymore
because I made Miss Arita mad?!

00:16:45.980 --> 00:16:47.550
That's not it.

00:16:47.550 --> 00:16:51.890
If I'm around, I'll cause
trouble for the people around me.

00:16:51.890 --> 00:16:57.160
I wanted to see you released from
the hospital, but it looks like I can't.

00:16:57.160 --> 00:16:58.460
Goodbye.

00:16:58.460 --> 00:17:00.450
Nataru, wait a second!

00:17:07.470 --> 00:17:11.460
"I'm out researching a story and I won't be back
until late. You can tell me what happened then.
- Muroto" <i>"PS:</i> Take some medicine."

00:17:12.810 --> 00:17:16.210
Stuff like that doesn't work anymore, Mr. Muroto.

00:17:27.820 --> 00:17:31.420
Pathetic... I don't even
have the strength left to jump?

00:17:51.450 --> 00:17:55.280
Yes, I heard you were coming.
It's Room 3 on the fourth floor.

00:17:55.280 --> 00:17:56.890
Thank you.

00:17:56.890 --> 00:17:58.050
Is he in the hospital?

00:17:58.050 --> 00:18:00.090
Huh? Uh, yeah...

00:18:00.090 --> 00:18:05.130
He's a lucky guy, having such
a cute girlfriend tending to him.

00:18:05.130 --> 00:18:08.260
I'm not his girlfriend. We're just friends.

00:18:08.260 --> 00:18:10.890
Aw, you don't have to hide it from me!

00:18:13.070 --> 00:18:15.540
Going into her boyfriend's
apartment for the first time

00:18:15.540 --> 00:18:18.740
would normally make a girl's heart flutter...

00:18:18.740 --> 00:18:21.080
Like I said, he's just a friend.

00:18:21.080 --> 00:18:23.070
Oh <i>really,</i> Ma'am?

00:18:34.560 --> 00:18:37.150
Birdy, isn't that blood?!

00:18:39.230 --> 00:18:43.130
Hello, this is Shion Arita, yessiree!

00:18:43.130 --> 00:18:45.670
Birdy, it's me.

00:18:45.670 --> 00:18:47.070
Nataru?

00:18:47.070 --> 00:18:48.900
I've got a favor to ask you.

00:18:48.900 --> 00:18:52.010
It's dangerous, so you're the only one I can turn to.

00:18:52.010 --> 00:18:55.440
What in the world's going on?

00:18:55.440 --> 00:18:57.280
Have a nice night!

00:18:57.980 --> 00:19:01.180
Would you bring me the
medicine from my apartment?

00:19:01.180 --> 00:19:02.250
More importantly...

00:19:02.250 --> 00:19:03.850
There's a chance you may be attacked.

00:19:03.850 --> 00:19:04.840
Huh?

00:19:24.970 --> 00:19:29.110
The inspector came out. Shall I follow her?

00:19:29.110 --> 00:19:34.710
You're no match for her.
Continue the stakeout like a good boy.

00:19:38.350 --> 00:19:41.560
Colonel, how are things there?

00:19:41.560 --> 00:19:45.290
They say he sent in a letter of resignation.

00:19:45.290 --> 00:19:47.460
Looks like he means to go into hiding.

00:19:47.460 --> 00:19:48.960
What now?

00:19:48.960 --> 00:19:54.070
He's looking for us, too.
Sooner or later he'll show himself again.

00:19:54.070 --> 00:19:55.970
This is a war of attrition now.

00:19:55.970 --> 00:19:59.670
A war, eh? Things are becoming fun.

00:19:59.670 --> 00:20:03.510
Yes. It's been a long time since
we took to the battlefield together.

00:20:18.190 --> 00:20:20.230
Was everything okay, Birdy?

00:20:20.230 --> 00:20:22.200
I'm just fine.

00:20:22.200 --> 00:20:25.100
But what kind of medicine is this?

00:20:25.100 --> 00:20:26.540
Sorry to cause you trouble.

00:20:26.540 --> 00:20:28.000
What's wrong, Nataru?

00:20:28.000 --> 00:20:31.910
What do you mean, someone's
after you? And that medicine...

00:20:31.910 --> 00:20:33.280
Nataru!

00:20:33.280 --> 00:20:37.080
I don't want to tell you.
You wouldn't believe me if I did.

00:20:37.080 --> 00:20:40.070
You really think I wouldn't believe you?!

00:20:45.850 --> 00:20:48.420
How did that happen?

00:20:48.420 --> 00:20:51.530
I'll tell you everything that happened.

00:20:51.530 --> 00:20:55.930
I don't want to say it too loudly,
so would you lean your face this way?

00:21:12.910 --> 00:21:14.110
Goodbye.

00:21:20.560 --> 00:21:24.660
Birdy, shouldn't you follow him?!
He was acting weird!

00:21:24.660 --> 00:21:27.460
I know. But...

00:21:27.460 --> 00:21:29.660
You love him, don't you?!

00:21:33.670 --> 00:21:34.660
Birdy?

00:21:35.270 --> 00:21:37.100
Birdy!

00:21:41.480 --> 00:21:46.310
<i>Only a love that's ended becomes a seed</i>

00:21:46.310 --> 00:21:52.510
<i>Next, a flower blooms</i>

00:22:04.100 --> 00:22:09.600
<i>If you hang your head like that,</i>
<i>you won't get any sunlight</i>

00:22:09.600 --> 00:22:15.140
<i>Look up at the blue sky so you'll grow taller!</i>

00:22:15.140 --> 00:22:20.820
<i>Let's pour a few tears from the watering can</i>

00:22:20.820 --> 00:22:26.810
<i>Eventually shoots will spring up</i>
<i>from somewhere in your heart</i>

00:22:29.460 --> 00:22:32.530
<i>Let's take life slowly</i>

00:22:32.530 --> 00:22:37.530
<i>A girl's dreams are neverending</i>

00:22:37.530 --> 00:22:43.740
<i>Ah, there's someone</i>
<i>out there waiting for you</i>

00:22:43.740 --> 00:22:48.580
<i>Only a love that's ended becomes a seed</i>

00:22:48.580 --> 00:22:55.250
<i>Next, a flower blooms</i>

00:22:55.250 --> 00:23:00.060
<i>Only a love that's ended becomes a seed</i>

00:23:00.060 --> 00:23:06.050
<i>Next, a flower blooms</i>

00:23:12.730 --> 00:23:16.370
<i>Nataru has gained the power to transcend time.</i>

00:23:16.370 --> 00:23:21.370
<i>But in exchange for that power,</i>
<i>his life is steadily whittled away.</i>

00:23:22.110 --> 00:23:26.380
<i>When Birdy finds out Muroto is taking care of him...</i>

00:23:26.380 --> 00:23:30.780
<i>And there Nataru has found a new target...</i>

00:23:33.250 --> 00:23:36.690
Please stop this, Nataru. I...
